Description: Test the ssl module against OpenSSL 4
 OpenSSL 4 still negotiates TLS 1.2 but no longer has the version-specific
 TLSv1_2_method, so ssl.PROTOCOL_TLSv1_2 raises ValueError while
 ssl.HAS_TLSv1_2 is true. has_tls_protocol() inferred the first from the
 second; it now also constructs the context. The two tests that used
 PROTOCOL_TLSv1_2 without asking has_tls_protocol() ask it, and
 test_openssl_version accepts OpenSSL 4. Pairs with
 openssl4-version-methods.patch.
Author: Peios maintainers <packaging@peios.org>
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no

--- a/Lib/test/test_ssl.py
+++ b/Lib/test/test_ssl.py
@@ -195,7 +195,16 @@
         # auto-negotiate protocols are always available
         return True
     name = protocol.name
-    return has_tls_version(name[len('PROTOCOL_'):])
+    if not has_tls_version(name[len('PROTOCOL_'):]):
+        return False
+    # A version can be enabled while its version-specific method is not:
+    # OpenSSL 4 negotiates TLS 1.2 but no longer has TLSv1_2_method.
+    try:
+        with warnings_helper.check_warnings():
+            ssl.SSLContext(protocol)
+    except ValueError:
+        return False
+    return True
 
 
